[1;36m==>[0m 1. composition.py's own asserts (compose, render faithfulness, verify, the CLI, priced deltas, the one remaining refusal)
OK compose(): the real driftwood composes against its real pinned parents; platform's two formerly-dangling claims are fixed, zero refusals
OK document: carries outcome, parents[], members[], refusals[], restatements[], cages[], holes[], ungoverned[], prices[], deltas[], limits[]
OK prices[]: computed on the real driftwood's very first composition too, with no prior signed artefact to compare a bump against -- old and new both price at this run's own pin, an honest 'no move'
OK prices[]: every entry names its perspective, currency, source and kind, and restates its own amount per customer against driftwood's OWN signed size (240000 customers)
OK prices[]: the insurer's signed quote books as one `premium` cost line under driftwood's own perspective (113403.30 GBP), and the insurer's layer arithmetic stays under its own
OK prices[]: a quote insuring another party, or booking its premium on another party's sheet, refuses as a missing instrument and prices nothing
OK exposure: driftwood's composed artefact signs its total priced exposure (3704381.74 GBP), its appetite as the attachment and the 3 breakdown by regime name and control id; the premium it buys is a cost and is not counted in it
OK pin signature: the real driftwood's quote pin resolves to the insurer's signed tag v1.0.0 on the checkout, and carries no hole
OK pin signature: only a checkout that can show the publisher's tag namespace may say `untagged` -- no tag at all, a lightweight tag and a flattened annotated tag all read `unobserved`; an annotated tag with no signature block is untagged
OK untagged pin: a quote pinned at a version no tag on the insurer's checkout signs composes (no refusal) with a hole of its own premium (113403.30 GBP) under driftwood's perspective, printed as a new-untagged-pin delta
OK untagged pin: a second composition records the hole and prints no delta
OK unobserved pin: a parent tree with no git metadata, and a checkout carrying no tag at all, both read `unobserved` -- they keep a recorded hole and open none, a could-not-look and never a signature
OK unobserved pin: a real signed tag flattened onto its commit by a second fetch reads `unobserved` and books NO hole -- a fabricated hole is worse than a missed one, and the fetch is the workflow's to fix (ticket 69)
OK closed pin: composing against the insurer's real signed tag closes the hole, prints one closed-untagged-pin delta, and the next composition carries no hole -- the hole heals itself when the tag lands
OK untagged pin: the rendered artefact is byte-identical across untagged, recorded and unobserved -- signature state lives in the evidence, never the render
OK prices[]: the one summing helper refuses a list that crosses a perspective or a currency -- no number in this estate is a lie by addition
OK prices[]: driftwood's own forward-intel feed prices as one source:twin entry -- perspective driftwood, GBP, tail bounded-pert, curve sha256:70e5e, policy version 1.1.0
OK prices[]: an adopter with no forward-intel feed simply has no twin entry -- a missing twin feed is never a refusal (ticket 25)
OK prices[]: an ico pin at v3 carries the published control weights as a per-hole breakdown -- 4 holes, weights sum to 1.0, and the entry amount IS the sum of the hole amounts (a hole partitions the regime, it never adds to it)
OK prices[]: an adopter with no signed appetite refuses as a missing instrument (ADR-0020), naming the artefact that declares none -- and prices nothing
OK prices[]: driftwood's own overlay.floor clamps the selection UP -- the threat-register price that picks baseline unclamped is held at the declared quarantine floor, tighten-only (ADR-0022)
OK limits[]: the two-publisher-conflict limit prints open at driftwood's one pinned implementations publisher
OK parents[]: all five declared parent kinds resolve to a non-empty SHA
OK load_implementations: cage-tier and cage-netpol, one family, one version, both survive (ADR-0016's fix for the prototype's (family, version) key)
OK load_implementations: a dedicated fixture, two members of one family at one version, both keys present
OK render_is_faithful: every member of every live version (10 total) renders back byte-identical after the header is stripped
OK render_member: no validationActions field written onto cage-tier (Mutating) or cage-netpol (Generating)
OK guards: orphan guard and governed-namespace-requires-claim both compose under the platform tag (no policy-version), rendering back to their offline twins' output
OK HEADER.yaml/holes[]: the real estate's first composition records 285 holes, all recorded (none new, none refused), ac-6.10 found by walking nested controls, and ac-6/cm-6 are covered (a claim exists, even the dangling one)
OK ungoverned[]: real driftwood's own namespace already carries governed: "true", so composition records zero ungoverned namespaces
OK verify(): a freshly composed and committed tree re-renders clean
OK verify(): a tampered committed file is caught as a byte-for-byte mismatch
